From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: simple-card: power down PineTab-V on close

ES8316 opts in to the ASoC power-down delay, which defaults to five
seconds after playback closes. On PineTab-V that also keeps its two
battery-fed TT8642 speaker amplifiers enabled, prolonging the reported
noise after application playback has stopped.

Ignore the delayed power-down only for the PineTab-V soundcard. Digital
mute and the ordered DAPM shutdown still run; other simple-card users keep
their existing delay. Userspace remains responsible for closing its PCM
when idle.

Link: https://files.pine64.org/doc/PineTab/PineTab-V_Schematic_Ver2-20240730.pdf
Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c b/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c
--- a/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c
+++ b/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c
@@ -220,6 +220,10 @@
 
 	dai_link->init			= simple_util_dai_init;
 	dai_link->ops			= &simple_ops;
+
+	/* Do not leave the battery-fed speaker amplifiers enabled after close. */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "pine64,pinetab-v-soundcard"))
+		dai_link->ignore_pmdown_time = 1;
 
 	ret = simple_util_set_dailink_name(priv, dai_link, name);
 end:
